                        \\begin{eqnarray}
                        n(A\\cup B\\cup C) &=& n(A) + n(B) + n(C)\\\\
                        &-& n(A\\cap B) - n(B\\cap C) - n(C\\cap A)\\\\
                        &+& n(A\\cap B\\cap C)
                        \\end{eqnarray}
                           \\]`)}</p></div></section> <section><h3 data-svelte-h="svelte-183jr9r">Examples</h3> <p class="examples">Let ${escape(`\\(A = \\{1, 2, 3\\}\\)`)} and ${escape(`\\(B = \\{2, 3, 4\\}\\)`)}, then ${escape(`\\(A\\cup B = \\{1, 2, 3, 4\\}, A\\cap B = \\{2, 3\\}\\)`)}. Therefore, ${escape(`\\[
                \\begin{eqnarray}
                n(A\\cup B) &=& n(A) + n(B) - n(A\\cap B)\\\\
                &=& 3 + 3 - 2 = 4
                \\end{eqnarray}
                 \\]`)}</p></section> </article>`;
